rnational treaty aimed at protecting human rights in the biomedical field.", "DEPARTMENT OF HEALTH:The Department of Health is a governmental department in the UK responsible for public health and health services.", "DR. MIKE STROUD:Dr. Mike Stroud is the director of the Department of Nutrition in Southampton, known for his work on clinical management in detention settings.", "BIOÉTICA:Bioética refers to the study of ethical issues arising from advances in biology and medicine, particularly in healthcare.", "JURISPRUDENCIA:Jurisprudencia refers to the body of court decisions that interpret laws and can influence future legal cases, including those related to medical ethics and prisoners' rights.", "HASTING CENTER REPORT:The Hasting Center Report is a publication that discusses ethical issues in medicine and healthcare, including priorities in medical practice.", "FUNDACIÓ VÍCTOR GRÍFOLS I LUCAS:Fundació Víctor Grífols i Lucas is an organization that publishes works related to medical ethics and bioethics, including the importance of nutrition in clinical settings.", "SOCIETY OF SPANISH PARENTERAL AND ENTERAL NUTRITION:The Society of Spanish Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition is an organization dedicated to enhancing nutritional support in clinical settings. It emphasizes specialized nutritional support and addresses the ethical aspects associated with this field. Through its initiatives, the society aims to improve the quality of care provided to patients requiring parenteral and enteral nutrition.", "TERRI SCHIAVO:Terri Schiavo was a woman whose case raised significant ethical questions regarding life support and artificial nutrition.", "ELUANA ENGLARO:Eluana Englaro was a woman whose case involved the withdrawal of artificial nutrition and hydration, sparking ethical debates."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}